GitHub issues.\\n00007| \\n00008| ## Test Issue\\n00009| An issue will be created asking to implement a \\\"Hello World\\\" program in Scala.\\n00010| \\n00011| ## Repository Status\\n00012| - **Created**: 2026-10-17T16:58:44.542Z\\n00013| - **Language**: Scala\\n00014| - **Type**: Test repository\\n00015| \\n\\n(End of file - total 15 lines)\\n</file>\",\"name\":\"read\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-abb3db47-cf5b-4be4-9693-b0b690ed4efa\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"content\\\":\\\"/**\\\\n * HelloWorld.scala\\\\n * \\\\n * A simple Scala program that prints \\\\\\\"Hello, World!\\\\\\\" to the console.\\\\n * \\\\n * To run this program:\\\\n *   1. Compile: scalac HelloWorld.scala\\\\n *   2. Run: scala HelloWorld\\\\n * \\\\n * Alternatively, you can run it directly with `scala HelloWorld.scala` (if using Scala 2.11 or later).\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nobject HelloWorld {\\\\n  def main(args: Array[String]): Unit = {\\\\n    println(\\\\\\\"Hello, World!\\\\\\\")\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\",\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792256348663/HelloWorld.scala\\\"}\"}}],\"reasoning\":\"Now, we need to create the Scala file and the workflow.\\n\\nLet's create the Scala file first. We'll create it in the root directory as HelloWorld.scala.\\n\\nWe'll write a simple object with a main method that prints \\\"Hello, World!\\\".\\n\\nWe'll also add comments and possibly a build/run instruction.\\n\\nSince the issue says: \\\"If applicable, include build/run instructions in a comment at the top of the file\\\"\\n\\nWe can include instructions for running with `scala` or `scalac` and `scala`.\\n\\nLet's create the file.\",\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now, we need to create the Scala file and the workflow.\\n\\nLet's create the Scala file first. We'll create it in the root directory as HelloWorld.scala.\\n\\nWe'll write a simple object with a main method that print