us checks or if the CI has started running. Let me check for any recent workflow runs or status checks.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-6f75dd11-bbb6-42cd-ab40-7390dbde63c8\",\"content\":\"{\\\"statusCheckRollup\\\":[]}\\n\",\"name\":\"bash\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-919bfc13-c96e-4a9a-ab06-1e518d17d72e\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"ls -la ci/\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"List contents of ci directory\\\"}\"}}],\"reasoning\":\"The status check rollup is still empty, which means the CI hasn't started yet or hasn't reported back. This could be because:\\n\\n1. The test harness that copies workflow files to .github/workflows/ hasn't processed it yet\\n2. There might be a delay in the CI system picking up the workflow\\n3. The workflow might need to be triggered manually or there's an issue with it\\n\\nLet me check if there are any workflow runs in the repository that might be related to our changes. I'll also verify that our workflow file exists and is correctly formatted.\",\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The status check rollup is still empty, which means the CI hasn't started yet or hasn't reported back. This could be because:\\n\\n1. The test harness that copies workflow files to .github/workflows/ hasn't processed it yet\\n2. There might be a delay in the CI system picking up the workflow\\n3. The workflow might need to be triggered manually or there's an issue with it\\n\\nLet me check if there are any workflow runs in the repository that might be related to our changes. I'll also verify that our workflow file exists and is correctly formatted.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-919bfc13-c96e-4a9a-ab06-1e518d17d72e\",\"content\":\"total 12\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 box box 4096 Oct 17 17:00 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 box box 4096 Oct 17 17:05 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 box box  743 Oct 17 17:02 test-hello-world.yml\\n\",\"name\":\"bash\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-980c4d53-2128-43ba-aec0-7ccb5bd2298f\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"read\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Read the workflow file to verify content\\\",\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792256348663/ci/test-hello-world.yml\\\"}\"}}],\"reasoning\":\"The workflow file exists. Let me double-check its content to make sure it's correct.\",\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The workflow file exists. Let me double-check its content to make sure it's correct.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-980c4d53-2128-43ba-aec0-7ccb5bd2298f\",\"content\":\"<file>\\n00001| name: Test Hello World Scala\\n00002| \\n00003| on:\\n00004|   push:\\n00005|     branches: [ main ]\\n00006|   pull_request:\\n00007|     branches: [ main ]\\n00008| \\n00009| jobs:\\n00010|   build-and-test:\\n00011|     runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n00012|     steps:\\n00013|       - uses: actions/checkout@v4\\n00014| \\n00015|       - name: Set up Scala\\n00016|         uses: scala-lang/setup-scala@v1\\n00017|         with:\\n00018|           scala-version: \\\"2.13.12\\\"\\n00019| \\n00020|       - name: Compile and run HelloWorld\\n00021|         run: |\\n00022|           scalac HelloWorld.scala\\n00023|           scala HelloWorld\\n00024| \\n00025|       - name: Verify output\\n00026|         run: |\\n00027|           output=$(scala HelloWorld)\\n00028|           if [ \\\"$output\\\" = \\\"Hello, World!\\\" ]; then\\n00029|             echo \\\"Output matches expected value.\\\"\\n00030|           else\\n00031|             echo \\\"Expected: 'Hello, World!'\\\"\\n00032|             echo \\\"Got: '$output'\\\"\\n00033|             exit 1\\n00034|           fi\\n\\n(End of file - total 34 lines)\\n</file>\",\"name\":\"read\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-2bcc3988-2f57-4be7-af58-203164a7e7be\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"gh api repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs?per_page=5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"List recent workflow runs\\\"}\"}}],\"reasoning\":\"The workflow looks correct. However, I notice that the `on` section specifies branches: [ main ], but our base branch is not main - it's \\\"e2e/hello-world/39050916672/agent-nemotron-3-super-free\\\". According to the issue requirements, the workflow should trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests. But since our base branch is not main, the workflow might not be triggering on pushes to our base branch.\\n\\nLet me re-read the issue requirements:\\n\\n\\\"The CI/CD workflow should:\\n- Trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests\\\"\\n\\nBut also from the issue:\\n\\\"Save the workflow as `ci/test-hello-world.yml`, not under `.github/workflows/`: this repository's token cannot push workflow files, so the test harness copies it there and runs it\\\"\\n\\nAnd from the initial instructions:\\n\\\"Requested by user --base-branch: e2e/hello-world/39050916672/agent-nemotron-3-super-free\\\"\\n\\\"The user expects the pull request base branch to remain e2e/hello-world/39050916672/agent-nemotron-3-super-free.\\\"\\n\\nThis suggests that the test harness will copy the workflow to .github/workflows/ and run it against the base branch. So even though our workflow says \\\"branches: [ main ]\\\", when the test harness copies it, it might adjust it or the system might be configured to run it regardless.\\n\\nHowever, to be safe and follow the exact requirement, I should check if I need to modify the workflow to trigger on the base branch instead of main, or if the test harness handles this.\\n\\nLooking at the issue description again:\\n\\\"The CI/CD workflow should:\\n- Trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests\\\"\\n\\nThis is a requirement for the workflow itself. But in this specific case, the base branch is not main. Let me check if there's any guidance on this.\\n\\nActually, looking at the issue more carefully, I think the workflow should be written to trigger on pushes to whatever the base branch is (which in a normal case would be main), and on pull requests. Since the test harness is going to copy this workflow to run against the specific base branch, I think the workflow as written is correct - it should trigger on pushes to main and on PRs. When the test harness runs it, it will be running in the context of a PR targeting the base branch.\\n\\nLet me wait a bit more to see if the CI starts, or check if there are any workflow runs at all in the repository that might give us a clue.\",\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The workflow looks correct. However, I notice that the `on` section specifies branches: [ main ], but our base branch is not main - it's \\\"e2e/hello-world/39050916672/agent-nemotron-3-super-free\\\". According to the issue requirements, the workflow should trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests. But since our base branch is not main, the workflow might not be triggering on pushes to our base branch.\\n\\nLet me re-read the issue requirements:\\n\\n\\\"The CI/CD workflow should:\\n- Trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests\\\"\\n\\nBut also from the issue:\\n\\\"Save the workflow as `ci/test-hello-world.yml`, not under `.github/workflows/`: this repository's token cannot push workflow files, so the test harness copies it there and runs it\\\"\\n\\nAnd from the initial instructions:\\n\\\"Requested by user --base-branch: e2e/hello-world/39050916672/agent-nemotron-3-super-free\\\"\\n\\\"The user expects the pull request base branch to remain e2e/hello-world/39050916672/agent-nemotron-3-super-free.\\\"\\n\\nThis suggests that the test harness will copy the workflow to .github/workflows/ and run it against the base branch. So even though our workflow says \\\"branches: [ main ]\\\", when the test harness copies it, it might adjust it or the system might be configured to run it regardless.\\n\\nHowever, to be safe and follow the exact requirement, I should check if I need to modify the workflow to trigger on the base branch instead of main, or if the test harness handles this.\\n\\nLooking at the issue description again:\\n\\\"The CI/CD workflow should:\\n- Trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests\\\"\\n\\nThis is a requirement for the workflow itself. But in this specific case, the base branch is not main. Let me check if there's any guidance on this.\\n\\nActually, looking at the issue more carefully, I think the workflow should be written to trigger on pushes to whatever the base branch is (which in a normal case would be main), and on pull requests. Since the test harness is going to copy this workflow to run against the specific base branch, I think the workflow as written is correct - it should trigger on pushes to main and on PRs. When the test harness runs it, it will be running in the context of a PR targeting the base branch.\\n\\nLet me wait a bit more to see if the CI starts, or check if there are any workflow runs at all in the repository that might give us a clue.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-2bcc3988-2f57-4be7-af58-203164a7e7be\",\"content\":\"{\\\"total_count\\\":10638,\\\"workflow_runs\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":39050916672,\\\"name\\\":\\\"E2E Hello World Matrix\\\",\\\"node_id\\\":\\\"WFR_kwLOPUU0qc8AAAAJF52zQA\\\",\\\"head_branch\\\":\\\"main\\\",\\\"head_sha\\\":\\\"b3b9a836731b5c7110340e267d26355fbef3bd08\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\".github/workflows/e2e-hello-world-matrix.yml\\\",\\\"display_title\\\":\\\"E2E Hello World Matrix\\\",\\\"run_number\\\":57,\\\"event\\\":\\\"workflow_run\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":null,\\\"workflow_id\\\":368825920,\\\"check_suite_id\\\":105830047373,\\\"check