github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}\\\",\\\"received_events_url\\\":\\\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"User\\\",\\\"user_view_type\\\":\\\"public\\\",\\\"site_admin\\\":false},\\\"jobs_url\\\":\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/39050754738/jobs\\\",\\\"logs_url\\\":\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/39050754738/logs\\\",\\\"check_suite_url\\\":\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/check-suites/105829612068\\\",\\\"artifacts_url\\\":\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/39050754738/artifacts\\\",\\\"cancel_url\\\":\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/39050754738/cancel\\\",\\\"rerun_url\\\":\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/39050754738/rerun\\\",\\\"previous_attempt_url\\\":null,\\\"workflow_url\\\":\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/workflows/350256528\\\",\\\"head_commit\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"7c63ee5e800f2c5b71b3a28efffba7dc557ab71f\\\",\\\"tree_id\\\":\\\"b3b37f1052b4dd20d813cd9201ac00bc9b621330\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"Repair v2.39.0, published with the old formatter while this PR was open (#3445)\\\\n\\\\nv2.39.0 lost its indentation, so its eight nested bullets became top-level\\\\nbullets. It was repaired with scripts/repair-release-notes.mjs after merging\\\\nmain. Its body b\\n\\n(Output was truncated due to length limit)\",\"name\":\"bash\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-fca01564-4658-4f2a-89c8-db3366b83add\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"sleep 30\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Wait longer for CI to potentially start\\\"}\"}}],\"reasoning\":\"I can see there are many workflow runs, but I don't see our specific workflow \\\"Test Hello World Scala\\\" in the list yet. This suggests that either:\\n\\n1. The test harness hasn't picked up our workflow yet\\n2. Our workflow hasn't been triggered because it's not matching the branch criteria\\n3. There's a delay in the system\\n\\nLet me wait a bit longer and then check again. Also, let me verify that our workflow would trigger on a pull request (which we have). The workflow is configured to trigger on pull_request to branches: [ main ]. Our PR is targeting the base branch \\\"e2e/hello-world/39050916672/agent-nemotron-3-super-free\\\", not main.\\n\\nThis might be the issue! The workflow won't trigger on our PR because it's not targeting main.\\n\\nLet me re-read the issue requirements one more time:\\n\\n\\\"The CI/CD workflow should:\\n- Trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests\\\"\\n\\nIt doesn't specify which branch for pull requests, but the example shows:\\n\\\"on:\\n  push:\\n    branches: [ main ]\\n  pull_request:\\n    branches: [ main ]\\\"\\n\\nHowever, in the context of this specific issue, the base branch is not main. The user has explicitly requested that the base branch remain \\\"e2e/hello-world/39050916672/agent-nemotron-3-super-free\\\".\\n\\nI think there are two possibilities:\\n1. The test harness will modify the workflow when copying it to match the base branch\\n2. I need to adjust the workflow to target the correct base branch\\n\\nLet me check if there are any examples in the repository of workflows that target non-main branches, or look for guidance.\\n\\nActually, let me think about this differently. The issue says:\\n\\\"Save the workflow as `ci/test-hello-world.yml`, not under `.github/workflows/`: this repository's token cannot push workflow files, so the test harness copies it there and runs it\\\"\\n\\nThis suggests that the test harness will take our workflow file and copy it to .github/workflows/ in the repository, and then run it. When it does this copying, it might adjust the branches to match the target base branch.\\n\\nGiven that the user has explicitly set th