[2026-10-17T17:12:35.264Z] [INFO]             "text": "I'm starting to think that maybe the test harness doesn't use the standard GitHub Actions triggering mechanism at all. Perhaps it has a different way of running workflows.\n\nLet me think about what the test harness might do:\n1. It checks out the repository\n2. It copies the workflow from ci/ to .github/workflows/\n3. Then it might run the workflow using the GitHub Actions API to create a workflow dispatch\n4. Or it might simulate the workflow execution in some other way\n\nIf it's using workflow dispatch, then our workflow would need to have a workflow_dispatch trigger, or it would be triggered automatically.\n\nActually, let me check if there are any other events I should be considering. Or perhaps the test harness runs on a schedule or is triggered by the PR creation/update.\n\nLet me look at the initial issue again to see if there are any hints about how the test harness works.\n\nThe issue says: \"this repository's token cannot push workflow files, so the test harness copies it there and runs it\"\n\nThis suggests that the test harness has special permissions or a special way to run workflows that doesn't require pushing to .github/workflows/.\n\nPerhaps the test harness:\n1. Has permission to create workflow runs\n2. Takes our workflow content\n3. Temporarily creates a workflow in the repository (via API)\n4. Runs it\n5. Then removes it\n\nOr maybe it uses the repository's default workflow permissions in a special way.\n\nLet me try adding a workflow_dispatch trigger to our workflow, which would allow manual triggering, and see if that helps the test harness somehow.",
[2026-10-17T17:12:35.264Z] [INFO]             "format": "unknown",
