al way to run workflows that doesn't require pushing to .github/workflows/.\\n\\nPerhaps the test harness:\\n1. Has permission to create workflow runs\\n2. Takes our workflow content\\n3. Temporarily creates a workflow in the repository (via API)\\n4. Runs it\\n5. Then removes it\\n\\nOr maybe it uses the repository's default workflow permissions in a special way.\\n\\nLet me try adding a workflow_dispatch trigger to our workflow, which would allow manual triggering, and see if that helps the test harness somehow.\",\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"I'm starting to think that maybe the test harness doesn't use the standard GitHub Actions triggering mechanism at all. Perhaps it has a different way of running workflows.\\n\\nLet me think about what the test harness might do:\\n1. It checks out the repository\\n2. It copies the workflow from ci/ to .github/workflows/\\n3. Then it might run the workflow using the GitHub Actions API to create a workflow dispatch\\n4. Or it might simulate the workflow execution in some other way\\n\\nIf it's using workflow dispatch, then our workflow would need to have a workflow_dispatch trigger, or it would be triggered automatically.\\n\\nActually, let me check if there are any other events I should be considering. Or perhaps the test harness runs on a schedule or is triggered by the PR creation/update.\\n\\nLet me look at the initial issue again to see if there are any hints about how the test harness works.\\n\\nThe issue says: \\\"this repository's token cannot push workflow files, so the test harness copies it there and runs it\\\"\\n\\nThis suggests that the test harness has special permissions or a special way to run workflows that doesn't require pushing to .github/workflows/.\\n\\nPerhaps the test harness:\\n1. Has permission to create workflow runs\\n2. Takes our workflow content\\n3. Temporarily creates a workflow in the repository (via API)\\n4. Runs it\\n5. Then removes it\\n\\nOr maybe it uses the repository's default workflow permissions in a special way.\\n\\nLet me try adding a workflow_dispatch trigger to our workflow, which would allow manual triggering, and see if that helps the test harness somehow.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-ee38cda4-3b5d-4f5a-8f13-6c67c30fd1cc\",\"content\":\"\",\"name\":\"edit\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-ab2957c7-3f47-49a8-b6d0-e1c9d3207397\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"git add ci/test-hello-world.yml\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Stage the updated workflow file\\\"}\"}}],\"reasoning_details\":[]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-ab2957c7-3f47-49a8-b6d0-e1c9d3207397\",\"content\":\"\",\"name\":\"bash\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-1fe6b8b5-ef63-46f4-abc6-80c93e340835\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"git commit -m \\\\\\\"Add workflow_dispatch trigger to GitHub Actions workflow\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Commit the workflow update\\\"}\"}}],\"reasoning\":\"Now let me commit and push.\",\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now let me commit and push.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-1fe6b8b5-ef63-46f4-abc6-80c93e340835\",\"content\":\"[issue-3487-f4cf27ad1f94 0213766c6] Add workflow_dispatch trigger to GitHub Actions workflow\\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)\\n\",\"name\":\"bash\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-fa0ab410-33c9-4f20-8a7f-a99651baf392\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"git push origin issue-3487-f4cf27ad1f94\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Push the updated workflow\\\"}\"}}],\"reasoning\":\"Now let me push and wait.\",\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text