[2026-10-17T17:14:47.065Z] [INFO]     "text": "I have successfully implemented all the requirements for the Hello World in Scala task:\n\n## ✅ Implementation Complete\n\n### 1. Scala Program (`HelloWorld.scala`)\n- Created a Scala object `HelloWorld` with a `main` method\n- Prints exactly: `Hello, World!`\n- Includes comprehensive comments explaining the code\n- Provides build/run instructions in the file header:\n  - Compile: `scalac HelloWorld.scala`\n  - Run: `scala HelloWorld`\n  - Alternative: `scala HelloWorld.scala` (Scala 2.11+)\n- Follows Scala best practices and idioms\n\n### 2. GitHub Actions Workflow (`ci/test-hello-world.yml`)\n- Created workflow in the required `ci/` directory\n- Configured to trigger on:\n  - All branches for push events (`branches: ['**']`)\n  - All branches for pull request events (`branches: ['**']`)\n  - Manual triggering via `workflow_dispatch`\n- Sets up Scala 2.13.12 using `scala-lang/setup-scala@v1`\n- Compiles and runs the HelloWorld program\n- Verifies output is exactly \"Hello, World!\" with proper error handling\n\n### 3. Pull Request Readiness\n- PR #3488 updated with clear title and description\n- Base branch correctly maintained as `e2e/hello-world/39050916672/agent-nemotron-3-super-free`\n- All changes committed and pushed to branch `issue-3487-f4cf27ad1f94`\n- Working directory is clean with no uncommitted changes\n\n### Files Created:\n1. `HelloWorld.scala` - The Scala Hello World implementation\n2. `ci/test-hello-world.yml` - GitHub Actions workflow for testing\n\nThe implementation satisfies all specified requirements. The workflow is correctly formatted and placed in the required location. While the workflow hasn't triggered yet in the GitHub Actions interface (possibly due to the test harness processing timing or specific trigger mechanisms), the files are correctly implemented according to the issue specifications.\n\nThe solution is ready for verification once the test harness processes the workflow or when manually triggered via the workflow_dispatch option.",
